        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.119,
            0.661,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": "Can you find a similar pictorial explanation?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.353,
            0.196,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.353,
            0.353,
            0.376
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.385,
            0.828,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "1. Can you find a similar pictorial explanation for why adding counting numbers up and down, i.e., 1, 1 + 2 + 1, 1 + 2 + 3 + 2 + 1, …, gives square numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.839,
            0.373,
            0.94,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.451,
            0.887,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "2. By imagining a large version of your picture, or drawing it partially, as needed, can you see what will be the value of $1+2+3+\\cdots+99+100+99+\\cdots+3+2+12$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.516,
            0.885,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "3. Which sequence do you get when you start to add the All 1’s sequence up? What sequence do you get when you add the All 1’s sequence up and down?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.581,
            0.885,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "4. Which sequence do you get when you start to add the counting numbers up? Can you give a smaller pictorial explanation?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.625,
            0.885,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": "5. What happens when you add up pairs of consecutive triangular numbers? That is, take $1 + 3 , 3 + 6 , 6 + 1 0 , 1 0 + 1 5 ,$ … Which sequence do you get? Why? Can you explain it with a picture?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.69,
            0.885,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": "6. What happens when you start to add up powers of 2 starting with 1, i.e., take 1, 1 + 2, 1 + 2 + 4, 1 + 2 + 4 + 8, … ? Now add 1 to each of these numbers—what numbers do you get? Why does this happen?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.089,
            0.942,
            0.11,
            0.96
          ],
          "content": "8"
